{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01K5rq2bmzpJiffLPhEn96vZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 source water profiles are available. Now I have enough to finalize the review.\n\n# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] The startup configuration screen includes independently selectable fields for: source water profile, substrate preset, plant selection, filter on/off, light photoperiod, heater enabled + setpoint, aeration on/off, and initial shrimp count — `SelectionField` enum now has all 12 entries (Scenario, Size, Fill, SourceWater, Substrate, Plants, Filter, Light, Heater, Aeration, ShrimpCount, Launch) and `render_startup` displays all of them in the configuration list\n- [x] Source water field cycles through all 4 available profiles (`soft_acidic`, `moderate`, `hard_shrimp`, `ro_like`) independently of the scenario — `startup_source_water_ids()` delegates to `tank_data::source_water_ids()` which returns exactly these 4; the `adjust_left`/`adjust_right` methods cycle through them\n- [x] Substrate field cycles through at least 4 preset combinations: `inert_sand`, `inert_gravel`, `active_planted`, `active_planted + coarse_porous` — `StartupSubstratePreset::ALL` contains exactly these 4 variants\n- [x] Plant selection field allows choosing: `FastStem only`, `RootFeedingRosette only`, `Both guilds`, or `None` — `StartupPlantSelection::ALL` contains exactly these 4 variants\n- [x] Filter field toggles enabled/disabled (defaults to enabled) — `adjust_left`/`adjust_right` both toggle `filter_enabled`; default scenario loads with `filter_enabled: Some(true)`\n- [x] Light field cycles through photoperiod presets (`6h`, `8h`, `10h`, `12h`) — `StartupLightPreset::ALL` has these 4 values\n- [x] Heater field cycles through options: `Off`, `24°C`, `25°C`, `26°C` — `StartupHeaterPreset::ALL` has exactly these 4 variants with correct setpoints\n- [x] Aeration field toggles enabled/disabled (defaults to disabled) — toggle logic in `adjust_left`/`adjust_right`; default `aeration_enabled: false` for most scenarios\n- [x] Initial shrimp count field allows setting 0, 5, 10, 15, or 20 shrimp — `STARTUP_SHRIMP_COUNTS: [u32; 5] = [0, 5, 10, 15, 20]`\n- [x] Scenario field is retained but acts as a template — scenario selection still exists and drives default values for all override fields via `startup_defaults_for_scenario`\n- [x] When a scenario is changed, the override fields reset to that scenario's defaults — `set_scenario_index` calls `reset_template_fields()` which loads and applies the scenario's defaults\n- [x] The materialization path applies the user's hardware and stocking choices to the `TankState` after scenario materialization — `seeded_state_with_full_overrides` calls `materialize_scenario` then `apply_startup_overrides`\n- [x] A tank launched with heater enabled starts with `HeaterState.enabled = true` and the selected setpoint — `apply_startup_overrides` sets `state.hardware.heater.enabled = true` and `state.hardware.heater.setpoint_c = setpoint_c`\n- [x] A tank launched with initial shrimp count > 0 starts with that many adults in the `AnimalState` — `apply_startup_overrides` sets `state.animal = AnimalState::with_adults(count)`\n- [x] The startup summary panel updates to reflect the user's current selections — `render_startup` shows a \"Launch summary\" pane with geometry, source water, substrate, plants, filter, light, heater, aeration, and initial shrimp count\n- [x] All existing acceptance tests continue to pass — verified: all 52 workspace tests pass including the 7 existing materialization tests\n- [x] A new integration test verifies that a state materialized with heater enabled and 10 initial shrimp has `hardware.heater.enabled == true` and `animals.adults == 10` — `startup_overrides_apply_heater_and_initial_shrimp` in `startup_overrides.rs` asserts both; a second test `startup_overrides_replace_source_water_profile` verifies source water override\n\n## Notes\n- The `seeded_state_with_overrides` existing API is preserved as a backward-compatible wrapper around `seeded_state_with_full_overrides`, maintaining all existing callers\n- Substrate and plant builders were refactored into reusable helpers (`build_substrate_layers`, `build_plant_guilds`) to avoid code duplication between initial materialization and override application — clean decomposition\n- The `cycle_choice` generic helper avoids duplicated cycling logic across 8+ fields\n\n## Commit Message\nfeat(startup): add per-component equipment and stocking selection to TUI startup screen"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":54774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52f697db-0b88-4b75-8545-7f61b7d5c7dd","uuid":"667850a4-3f5c-4ad7-b7a0-7388e4b55f17"}
